From f916436fca88215cb0f442879586d1f1f1226021 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:49:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/27] Stop storing the market; fetch it live and keep only
 what was learned
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The store-and-read data plane was the root of two failures at once. Reading a
decade of bars for the whole universe out of a metered Postgres is the single
largest recurring egress in the system — it exhausted the free-tier transfer
quota — and once the writes could no longer land, every page went STALE because
freshness depended on a store a broken cron had stopped updating. Storing bulk
market data you can re-fetch for free is paying rent, in the one currency the
tier rations, for a copy of what the source gives away.

This inverts it. ingestion/live_provider.py fetches the universe's recent OHLCV
live from Yahoo (keyless, free), caches it in-process for the life of a warm
instance (tight TTL while NSE is open, loose after the close), and the snapshot
is built from those bars — the price panel is never read from or written to the
database on the hot path. What persists is only the tiny, hard-won state: the
few-hundred-KB computed snapshot and the KB-scale calibration ledger. Live data
in, compute and learn, keep the knowledge, discard the bulk, next cycle pulls
fresh — the data cannot go stale because it comes from the source, not a store.

Built to degrade honestly: a thin fetch (Yahoo throttling a cloud IP is real)
refuses to publish a hollow universe and falls back to the stored panel with the
reason stamped into the snapshot, never silent. Views self-refresh on the market
clock in live mode with no cron. Paper marks read the live cache when no bar is
stored, so the self-improving loop keeps running with nothing bulk persisted.
Enabled by default on hosted serverless (EQUISENSE_LIVE_DATA), off locally so dev
and tests stay offline; the DB path and every existing test are unchanged.

And seeding is disabled entirely — real data only, on every surface. The demo
generator that once fabricated fundamentals for real companies (and served 54
fake rows on a live fallback) is now a no-op that writes nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019SdgTAKohW7b1SaVZ9PVp6
