the same cashflows put into the index, the honest 'am I actually beating the
market' measure. It read the index from the stored macro table, which in live
mode is empty, so the benchmark and every alpha figure would silently disappear
exactly when the book is being judged.

The benchmark counterfactual now falls back to the live index series (dated, so
each trade is aligned to the index price on its own date, and the final mark is
the latest live close), and reports which source it used. The stored path is
unchanged; only the empty-store case reaches for live data.
