Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The user's recurring complaint was not being able to see the data refresh itself.
In stored mode that answer was the panel's age; in live mode there is no stored
panel, so freshness is the in-process cache's age on the market clock — a
different number that was computed nowhere the UI could reach. Data Health now
reports which mode is active, the plain-language reason it cannot go stale, and
the live cache's warmth and coverage, so 'is this fresh' is answerable at a
glance instead of inferred from a frozen screen.

It also surfaces the F&O executability provenance — the pinned short-eligibility
snapshot and its date — so the list that decides whether a bearish signal is
even actionable is visible and dated, never silently assumed current.
