The regime is read from stored macro (NIFTY, India VIX, USD/INR, Brent). In live
mode that table is empty, so classify_regime came back blank — and with it every
control that reads the regime went quiet: the VIX de-risk that halts new exposure
in stress, and the 200DMA market-trend filter that stops longs into a falling
market. The book would have run with its risk brakes silently disconnected in
exactly the mode just switched on, which is the most dangerous kind of gap
because nothing announces it.

_macro now fetches the index, VIX, FX and crude live when nothing is stored, so
the regime classifies normally and the de-risk and trend filters fire as designed.
A failed fetch returns empty and the regime degrades to 'unknown' exactly as
before — no new failure mode, just the brakes reconnected.
