Subject: [PATCH 18/27] Flag live-mode base rates as survivorship-biased, in
 the output
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The deep live panel that backs the studies in live mode is current-members-only,
so its base rates are survivorship-biased — winners dropped from the index are
absent, which flatters every long-side rate. The stored panel keeps delisted
names precisely to correct this, and the README leads with the corrected numbers.
Running the same studies on live data without saying so would quietly present
biased rates as if they carried the same discipline. The study result now carries
an explicit live-survivorship flag and names its panel source, so the two can
never be confused.
