Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review of the branch (code-review, high) surfaced one production-breaking
bug and four real defects, all fixed:

1. CRITICAL — qualified_candidates referenced an undefined `t` in the short
   executability block, so the FIRST bearish verdict raised NameError and 500'd
   the entire candidate scan, the autopilot run, and the live screen. The
   long-only test fixtures never produced a short, so nothing caught it. Fixed to
   `item["ticker"]` and added a regression test that forces a short verdict
   through and asserts a non-F&O name is refused while an F&O name is sized as a
   future.

2. Paper cost-drag double-charged (₹20 futures brokerage AND ₹15 DP on every
   sell) and applied the heavy delivery statutory rate to futures shorts,
   inflating the drag. Now a single, clearly-labelled delivery-basis estimate:
   one statutory side per leg plus the flat DP charge on sells.

3. get_universe's read-only status probe (allow_rebuild=False) wrote an empty
   snapshot into the 15s probe cache, so a real request arriving within the
   window got a blank universe instead of rebuilding. The non-rebuilt path no
   longer pollutes the cache.

4. get_universe re-parsed a corrupt stored payload unguarded after the guarded
   parse had already failed, 500-ing the status endpoint. It now reuses the
   already-parsed value or degrades to empty.

5. effective_breadth reported the post-history-filter count as the position
   count, understating holdings and inflating breadth efficiency when a held name
   lacked history. It now reports the true count and names how many were excluded.
