Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The README still described the store-and-read architecture as the design, which
would mislead an operator deploying today — the whole point of the rearchitecture
is that bulk market data is no longer stored. Added §3.1a documenting live-data
mode (free Yahoo fetch, in-process cache, nothing bulk persisted, self-refresh on
the market clock, cron writes nothing, deep studies on demand and survivorship-
flagged, honest fallback), the EQUISENSE_LIVE_DATA switch and its default, and the
env-var table + .env.example entry. The operator now sees the mode that actually
keeps the deployment inside the free-tier transfer allowance.
---
